      "correspondence": "The row's cross-block factors give ∏ b_j^(k−1), its negative-negative gaps cost nothing. Strip the 2k−3 endpoint factors from V(u); the remaining gaps inject into nonadjacent c gaps, and every unused c gap is at least one. Divide and take logs; the dimension comparison supplies 2/3, the place estimate budgets 5kL, and replacing (k−1)log b by k log w over the m terms costs ≤k+2kL. The algebra example has V(4,0,−3,−5)=7560 and V(6,2,−1)=84.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "Independent reader checked the example (ratio 90), 2/3, 5kL, k+2kL and the need for m/x≤1; its small ranks only model the interlacing comparison."
    },
